      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies:\n1. `ofTaiSeconds(-1L, -1L)` normalizes negative nanoseconds: TAI seconds becomes `-2` (floor division), nanos becomes `999_999_999` (floor modulo)\n2. `equals()` on a non-`TaiInstant` object returns `false`\n\nLet me write an improved version with descriptive names and clear intent.The improved test compiled successfully — descriptive variable names, inline comments explaining the negative-nano normalization math, and a Javadoc-style summary were added without altering any method calls or expected values."
